                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f7e9bf8-3b95-3701-accf-4e4cbaf24f19",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bout of heavy drinking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "612609ae-4348-4f37-8d92-8c349d6dd81c",
                                                "sense_id": "5f7e9bf8-3b95-3701-accf-4e4cbaf24f19",
                                                "text": "He's been out on a bender with his mates."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a54927b6-8864-4aa1-b48d-0956a6ac50b5",
                                                "sense_id": "5f7e9bf8-3b95-3701-accf-4e4cbaf24f19",
                                                "text": "A couple of students of Williams College went over to North Adams on a bender. This would have been serious matter under the best of circumstances, but each returned with a “brick in his hat,” etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7cbec3d-b3d0-4d14-8efc-9318cead6223",
                                                "sense_id": "5f7e9bf8-3b95-3701-accf-4e4cbaf24f19",
                                                "text": "\"Wait, is this about the other night when you two lightweights totally went on that bender?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aeb0af5e-cbe7-4eb2-9ef1-709a7e83abdf",
                                                "sense_id": "5f7e9bf8-3b95-3701-accf-4e4cbaf24f19",
                                                "text": "We can have a mad one, we can have a bender / Order what you want from the bartender / Come back to mine and all be splender / I'll give you a night to remember"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "353f1dce-0456-3e49-8e70-8746575518fb",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A homosexual man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56a56526-e430-444e-895f-5491f45ad520",
                                                "sense_id": "353f1dce-0456-3e49-8e70-8746575518fb",
                                                "text": "“So they're easy about having a bender in the house, are they, their lordships?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e783c19-a8af-3783-89d2-ceb34daec9d6",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A simple shelter, made using flexible branches or withies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8ec44fa-0608-345a-a249-ead51340aa8d",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A suspended sentence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d70bc2db-e5cc-4ee7-9626-33793ffebefb",
                                                "sense_id": "d8ec44fa-0608-345a-a249-ead51340aa8d",
                                                "text": "'Oh and Gary, what happened in Ahmed?' 'Not guilty, sir.' 'Oh no! And Tredwell?' 'Bender.' 'Suspended sentence? So both walked. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3df6517-302b-4009-a63b-86e36d955951",
                                                "sense_id": "d8ec44fa-0608-345a-a249-ead51340aa8d",
                                                "text": "He anticipated a prison sentence though he thought there was a slight possibility of 'getting off on a bender' (suspended sentence)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de2153a0-387a-38cc-b455-f3a5ee15eea6",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sixpence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9590d934-ca26-4472-87d8-22bd9ec1d4b2",
                                                "sense_id": "de2153a0-387a-38cc-b455-f3a5ee15eea6",
                                                "text": "What will you take to be paid out?’ said the butcher. ‘The regular chummage is two–and–six. Will you take three bob?’ ‘And a bender,’ suggested the clerical gentleman. ‘Well, I don’t mind that; it’s only twopence a piece more,’ said Mr. Martin. ‘What do you say, now? We’ll pay you out for three–and–sixpence a week. Come!’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3e04180-0f4d-3f98-b353-e4ff76e38c8f",
                                        "entry_id": "4ea8e505-52ad-3650-a2d9-b754ffbf1c83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A spree, a frolic."
                                        ],
